From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rvwasm <rvwasm@localhost>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:41:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] wasm: refuse a clone that is a fork

musl's fork() is clone(SIGCHLD) without a stack. The kernel took it, and the
child's Worker called __libc_clone_callback, which took a function and its
argument from the top of the parent's stack, where nobody had put them:
"table index is out of bounds", and the child died with SIGILL while the
parent saw a fork that had succeeded. Without an MMU there is no copy of the
parent's memory to give a child anyway; NOMMU kernels fail fork() with
EINVAL, and programs then take vfork() or posix_spawn().

A user clone with neither a new stack nor CLONE_VM now fails with EINVAL.
(Without a stack but with CLONE_VM, the C library has put the function on
the parent's stack, which the child borrows, CLONE_VFORK: that stays.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/wasm/kernel/process.c | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/wasm/kernel/process.c b/arch/wasm/kernel/process.c
index 6bdc5ff..7cfbbd7 100644
--- a/arch/wasm/kernel/process.c
+++ b/arch/wasm/kernel/process.c
@@ -208,7 +208,23 @@ int copy_thread(struct task_struct *p, const struct kernel_clone_args *args)
 		child_switch_stack->fn = args->fn;
 		child_switch_stack->fn_arg = args->fn_arg;
 	} else {
-		/* User thread */
+		/*
+		 * User thread. The child's Worker runs the C library's clone
+		 * callback (__libc_clone_callback), which takes the function to
+		 * call and its argument from the top of the child's stack: the
+		 * new stack, or without one the parent's (where the C library
+		 * has put them, and which the child borrows, as with vfork(),
+		 * CLONE_VM | CLONE_VFORK). A clone with neither a stack nor
+		 * CLONE_VM is a fork(), which has put nothing there, and
+		 * without an MMU there is no copy of the parent for it to
+		 * return into: refused, as fork() is on other kernels without
+		 * an MMU, so that the program can take another way
+		 * (posix_spawn()). Its child would otherwise call whatever the
+		 * parent's stack held there, and die.
+		 */
+		if (!args->stack && !(args->flags & CLONE_VM))
+			return -EINVAL;
+
 		*child_pt_regs = *parent_pt_regs;
 		if (args->stack)
 			child_pt_regs->stack_pointer = args->stack;
